[11:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the mask. That\'s better. Then I click animate to this state. And in a couple seconds, there it is. And everybody knows. And it works the same across all three surfaces. That\'s a perfectly smooth animation. Then in the'

[11:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'later section, I wanted that to move up to the center. So I\'ll put the playhead there. Click refresh frame so I can see where it needs to go. Click the location and shape again. Got to make sure that orange light is perfectly at the top.'

[11:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then click animate. And now here it is. Perfect. So now I\'ll make it bigger. Then I can play that from the beginning and you can see how the animations sync up with what I\'m saying. Chat is the one everybody knows and it works the same'

[12:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'across all three surfaces. This is your back and forth with Claude for brainstorming, writing, research, working out an idea. It\'s a thinking partner. You can extend it with built-in features like projects which give it'

[12:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'permanent context about your work or connectors which let it use your other tools like your email or your calendar or artifacts which is that little app or document window that opens next to the chat. But at its core, chat is a'

[12:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conversation. Everything chat does even when it makes you a file or builds you a little dashboard, it happens inside one turn, then it hands it back and waits for you.'

[12:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve used these in quite a few videos now, but it is still insane to me how easy it is to get this quality of motion graphics. But now I want to do one more example because there\'s still a really important feature I haven\'t covered yet.'

[12:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Uploading a series of reference images works great, but that only applies to that generation. A lot of the time, you\'ll want to use a style across multiple generations so it stays'

[13:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'consistent across shots or across videos. Maybe that\'s so it matches your brand colors every time. Or like me, I make a lot of videos about Claude and I want it to have the logo and UI and colors every time. Or even within a'

[13:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'single video, I usually only generate around 30 seconds or up to 2 minutes sections at a time. And I may have a few of those across a video. So I need to create a reusable design system, which is really easy. You can click the plus'

[13:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'button under the design system dropown or below there\'s a design system tab where you can see all of your previous systems. Then for a new one, click create design system. Then either create using cloud code or I\'ll show create'

[13:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here. Then you can link code from GitHub, your computer, upload a Figma file, or drop in the images you want it to draw from. I just dropped in these three images. I used GPT image 2 to generate these in a consistent style'

